==English==
{{wikipedia|phlogiston theory}}

===Etymology===
Coined by [[w:Georg Ernst Stahl|Stahl]] in 1702, from {{AGr.}} '''{{polytonic|[[φλογιστόν]]}}''', neuter of '''{{polytonic|[[φλογιστός]]}}''' ‘inflammable’, from '''{{polytonic|[[φλογίζειν]]}}''' ‘to set fire to’, from '''{{polytonic|[[φλόξ]]}}''' ‘flame’.

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|/flə(ʊ)ˈdʒɪstɒn/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{context|chemistry|historical}} The [[hypothetical]] [[fiery]] [[principle]] formerly assumed to be a necessary [[constituent]] of [[combustible]] bodies and to be given up by them in [[burning]].

====Related terms====
* [[dephlogisticated air]]

